world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto2) noble; urgency=medium

  * 18 more layouts, the ones that needed only a few keys: French, English
    (UK), Spanish, Portuguese, Portuguese (Brazil), Italian, Hungarian,
    Estonian, Lithuanian, Icelandic, Faroese, Albanian, Ukrainian, French
    (Canada, legacy), Norwegian, Danish, Finnish and Dutch. Not released.
  * Names now say "(as on Windows)": xkb-data already has layouts called
    "(Windows)" (for example Italian (Windows)), which are something else.
  * A key with characters on level 5 and up on Linux is left as on Linux.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Prototype: German, Swiss German, Swiss French and Polish (Programmers)
    layouts that type like Windows, next to the Linux layouts. Not released.
  * Lists the layouts in xkb-data's layout list (diverted, rebuilt after
    every xkb-data change), so Cinnamon (Linux Mint) can offer them.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
